window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"sylas","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Locke","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 2","text":"The lane hinges on him dodging your Q — land it and trades tilt your way."},{"when":"Level 6","text":"Your W heal and mobility offset his fresh ult in any extended fight."},{"when":"Locke first item","text":"Purgatory executes straight through the Kingslayer heal — stop trusting W to save you low."},{"when":"Two-plus items","text":"Ult-theft and mobility neutralise his single-target burst — even footing again."}],"wants":{"you":["Q landed before committing chains","W heals cashed at their strongest window","His own ult stolen and turned on him"],"foe":["Your Q side-stepped repeatedly","You anchored low where Purgatory reaches","Burst finished before your W lands"]},"early":"The whole laning phase is an even scrap: your Q poke trades into his on-hit pressure, and the exchanges hinge on landing skillshots, not stat checks. Poke with Q, take W-healed trades when his cooldowns lapse, and treat the coinflip stages as farm time — neither of you can force a decision yet.","mid":"At 6 your W heal and mobility offset his fresh ult in long fights, but his first item brings the lane's one hard lesson: Purgatory executes straight through the Kingslayer heal. The W-to-survive habit dies here — leave trades before the execute line, and remember his R is stealable with Hijack.","late":"With items it evens back out for good: your ult-theft and mobility neutralise a kit built on sticking single-target burst to one man. Dash through fights, steal whichever ult hurts his team most, and keep your HP above his threshold — an unexecutable Sylas is a problem he cannot solve.","whys":["Level 1 is even — your Q poke against his on-hit trades, no favourite.","At 2 the lane hinges on him dodging your Q, not on raw stats.","Level 3 stays even, revolving around your W-healed trades.","Through 4-5 short trades keep the matchup a coin-flip.","At 6 your W heal and mobility offset his fresh ult in a long fight.","At his first item Purgatory executes you through the Kingslayer heal — his stage.","With items your ult-theft and mobility neutralise his single-target burst — even again."]});
