window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"sylas","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Zaahen","Zaahen","Skill","Skill","Zaahen","Zaahen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Zaahen level 2","text":"He punishes you the instant Chain Lash is down — track your own E like a resource."},{"when":"Zaahen level 3","text":"His Q-E brawl beats your poke-on-cooldown pattern; keep everything at range."},{"when":"Your level 6","text":"Hijack can steal his all-in ult — his best button becomes your best button."},{"when":"Zaahen first item","text":"His durability and sustain out-value your poke — stop trading, start roaming."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke only behind Chain Lash cover","His R stolen for the counter all-in","Grievous Wounds bought before any all-in"],"foe":["Trades forced while your E is down","Extended brawls his Q and R heal through","A sidelane 1v1 at two items"]},"early":"Level 1 is quiet farming, then the squeeze starts: from 2 he punishes a squishy Sylas whenever Chain Lash is down, and by 3 Aureate Rush closes on 10 seconds and slices for percent health, so armour alone will not hold it. Treat E as your safety budget — poke only while it is up, and farm the even 4-5 window.","mid":"At 6 the lane reads even, and Hijack is why: his R is a kill button, and stealing it hands you the very all-in he planned to use on you. After his first item his durability and passive sustain out-value your poke, so stop trading — shove, roam with your mobility, and win the other lanes.","late":"At two-plus items he wins the sidelane 1v1, so give him the sidelane and take the game: you are a teamfight champion holding a stolen ult. Respect his 850-range stab — it pulls you in and starts everything else. Group, dash to the target that matters, and drop his own R on his team.","whys":["Level 1 is a farming skill check — his Q is an auto-reset, so read the wind-up.","At 2 his Q recast knocks you up whenever your Chain Lash is down.","Level 3 is his: the Q-E brawl beats your poke on cooldown.","Levels 4-5 read even as you both trade around your E windows.","Level 6 is a wash — Grim Deliverance kills and heals him, but you steal it off his 110-second cooldown.","At first item his Q heal and Determination stacks beat your squishy poke.","With 2+ items he wins the sidelane 1v1 — your value is teamfights and his stolen ult, not the duel."]});
